    "font" : "CMTI10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "after a fixed choice of parametrization of boundary of D by R. (In the case the end of D is negative, the above is meant to be analogous.)"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 4,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 85.039, 603.42, 526.966, 668.525 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "A Hamiltonian connection A on [0,1] × M uniquely corresponds to a choice of a smooth function H : [0,1] × M → R, normalized to have mean zero at each moment. For the holonomy path of A over [0,1] is a path ϕA : [0,1] → Ham(M,ω), generated by a Hamiltonian H : [0,1] × M → R, and this uniquely determines the connection. Conversely, H uniquely determines a Hamiltonian connection with holonomy path generated by H. We can say that H generates A."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 5,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 85.039, 555.271, 526.965, 597.815 ],
    "font" : "CMTI10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Lemma 2.26. Let p and Lp ⊂ ∂D × M be as in definition above with L±( p) = ρ, where p is some lift of p to Ham(M,ω), that is p(t) = p(t)(p(0)). Let A0 be a Hamiltonian connection on [0,1] × M, generated by a Hamiltonian H : [0,1] × M → R with L± length κ, constant for t near 0,1. Then"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 6,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 85.039, 537.188, 526.962, 561.652 ],
    "font" : "CMTI10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "there is a Hamiltonian connection Ap0 on D × M, preserving Lp, compatible with respect to A0, and satisfying"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 7,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 266.315, 517.155, 345.684, 536.737 ],
    "font" : "CMMI10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "area( Ap0) ≤ κ + ρ."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 8,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 85.039, 496.501, 526.963, 520.965 ],
    "font" : "CMTI10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The construction is natural in the sense that ( p,A0)  → Ap0 can be made into a smooth map (of Frechet manifolds)."
