    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 9,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 85.039, 434.885, 526.603, 482.207 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Proof. Let q : [0,1] → Ham(M,ω) be the holonomy path of A0, q(0) = id, generated by H. Let p · q be the usual path concatenation in diagrammatic order, and H′ be its generating Hamiltonian. Define a coupling form Ω′ on D2 × M:"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
